        "uuid": "e0fdd5ab_de1bc662",
        "filename": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Network/EthernetInterface.interface.yaml",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 21,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-21T07:28:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This configuration describes the hardware USB connectivity for each platform. Some platforms use only a BMC, while others connect the BMC to the host over USB. In some cases, two BMCs are connected to each other over USB (BMC1 ↔ BMC2).\n\nBecause this information is specific to the target platform and is known before the platform image is built, it can be configured in the phosphor-networkd meta-layer at build time. Therefore, this is appropriately handled as a build-time configuration.",
      "parentUuid": "50679f45_37102212",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 18,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 21,
        "endChar": 64
      },
      "revId": "713807d68fba394e4f3916ee0a5475e99fdf7df8",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0fd7ea69_b3c2753f",
        "filename": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Network/EthernetInterface.interface.yaml",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 21,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-21T11:19:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We are aiming to make everything configuration-based so that you can use the same BMC image on multiple platforms.  I don\u0027t see any reason to add a new compile time decision for this.",
      "parentUuid": "e0fdd5ab_de1bc662",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 18,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 21,
        "endChar": 64
      },
      "revId": "713807d68fba394e4f3916ee0a5475e99fdf7df8",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
